WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.723
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.023 --> 00:00:08.212
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.512 --> 00:00:13.603
Unit fifteen: Oceans. In this unit, you will talk about protecting the oceans.

4
00:00:14.617 --> 00:00:15.502
Ocean.

5
00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:19.478
Ocean means a very large area of salt water.

6
00:00:19.778 --> 00:00:21.685
The Pacific is the biggest ocean.

7
00:00:22.385 --> 00:00:24.538
Your turn. Say: Ocean.

8
00:00:27.238 --> 00:00:28.088
Ocean.

9
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:29.817
Wave.

10
00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:33.074
Wave means a moving line of water in the sea.

11
00:00:33.374 --> 00:00:34.735
The waves are big today.

12
00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.900
Your turn. Say: Wave.

13
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.311
Wave.

14
00:00:43.317 --> 00:00:44.329
Coral reef.

15
00:00:45.029 --> 00:00:48.782
Coral reef means an underwater place made of coral, home to many fish.

16
00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.942
Coral reefs are full of colour.

17
00:00:51.642 --> 00:00:53.772
Your turn. Say: Coral reef.

18
00:00:56.472 --> 00:00:57.624
Coral reef.

19
00:00:58.617 --> 00:00:59.362
Whale.

20
00:01:00.062 --> 00:01:02.619
Whale means a very large sea mammal.

21
00:01:02.919 --> 00:01:04.977
The blue whale is the biggest animal.

22
00:01:05.677 --> 00:01:07.969
Your turn. Say: Whale.

23
00:01:10.669 --> 00:01:11.380
Whale.

24
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:13.280
Pollution.

25
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:18.290
Pollution means dirty or harmful things in the air, water or land.

26
00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.694
Oil pollution kills sea birds.

27
00:01:21.394 --> 00:01:25.370
Your turn. Say: Pollution.

28
00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.024
Pollution.

29
00:01:30.017 --> 00:01:30.936
Plastic.

30
00:01:31.636 --> 00:01:34.809
Plastic means a light material used for bags and bottles.

31
00:01:35.109 --> 00:01:38.141
Plastic can stay in the sea for 400 years.

32
00:01:38.841 --> 00:01:41.563
Your turn. Say: Plastic.

33
00:01:44.263 --> 00:01:45.183
Plastic.

34
00:01:46.183 --> 00:01:46.964
Protect.

35
00:01:47.664 --> 00:01:49.838
Protect means to keep safe from harm.

36
00:01:50.138 --> 00:01:51.916
We must protect sea turtles.

37
00:01:52.616 --> 00:01:55.083
Your turn. Say: Protect.

38
00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:58.633
Protect.

39
00:01:59.617 --> 00:02:00.246
Deep.

40
00:02:00.946 --> 00:02:02.853
Deep means going a long way down.

41
00:02:03.153 --> 00:02:04.595
The ocean is very deep.

42
00:02:05.295 --> 00:02:07.808
Your turn. Say: Deep.

43
00:02:10.508 --> 00:02:11.138
Deep.

44
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.184
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:16.600
Sreypich, what lives in the ocean?

46
00:02:17.917 --> 00:02:19.847
Fish, turtles and huge whales!

47
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.417
What is the biggest problem for the oceans?

48
00:02:24.717 --> 00:02:28.112
Plastic pollution. Turtles eat plastic bags.

49
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:30.522
What must we do?

50
00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:35.035
We must reduce plastic, and we need to clean beaches.

51
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:38.872
Grammar focus: Must and need to.

52
00:02:39.172 --> 00:02:42.486
We must reduce plastic. We need to protect whales.

53
00:02:42.786 --> 00:02:48.120
'Must' and 'need to' both mean it is necessary. 'Need to' is a little softer.

54
00:02:49.117 --> 00:02:51.572
Now read and listen. Blue Planet.

55
00:02:51.872 --> 00:02:53.593
Oceans cover most of the Earth.

56
00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:59.402
Coral reefs are home to many fish, and whales live in the deep ocean.

57
00:03:00.717 --> 00:03:04.609
Plastic pollution is a big problem, and many sea animals are in danger.

58
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:08.299
We must reduce plastic and recycle more.

59
00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:11.920
We need to protect the oceans for the future.

60
00:03:13.217 --> 00:03:15.637
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:15.937 --> 00:03:17.588
We blank reduce plastic.

62
00:03:17.888 --> 00:03:21.994
A, must. B, musts. C, must to.

63
00:03:25.983 --> 00:03:27.646
The answer is A: must.

64
00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.883
We need blank protect whales.

65
00:03:31.183 --> 00:03:34.186
A, to. B, for. C, at.

66
00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:40.183
The answer is A: to.

67
00:03:41.683 --> 00:03:43.962
A very large sea mammal is a blank.

68
00:03:44.262 --> 00:03:47.160
A, whale. B, wave. C, reef.

69
00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.732
The answer is A: whale.

70
00:03:54.217 --> 00:03:57.740
Now it's your turn to speak. How can we protect the oceans?

71
00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:09.372
We must stop using plastic bags, and we need to clean beaches. We can also teach others about pollution.

72
00:04:09.672 --> 00:04:11.405
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:12.417 --> 00:04:16.184
Great work today! You learned eight new words and must and need to.

74
00:04:16.484 --> 00:04:21.040
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

75
00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.923
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:24.223 --> 00:04:27.572
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

